@extends('layouts/marketing')

@section('title', 'The Open Times — publish it, send it, own it')
@section('description', 'An independent paper you actually own: the publication, the newsletter and the paid subscriptions all run on software you host. Crossposts to every network. Open source, and nobody takes a cut.')
@section('canonical', 'https://theopentimes.org/')
@section('ogImage', 'https://theopentimes.org/images/og/home.png')

@section('content')

  <!--
    THE FRONT PAGE

    Laid out the way a broadsheet is rather than the way a landing page is: a
    banner headline across the full measure, a lede running in columns beneath
    it, and a boxed insert in the right-hand well. Everything below is another
    story on the same sheet, separated by printed rules rather than by cards
    floating over a background.
  -->
  <article class="mx-auto px-6 max-w-[1400px]">

    <!-- Lead story -->
    <section class="pt-10 sm:pt-14">
      <p class="text-center kicker">Late edition &middot; Open source &middot; Volume one</p>

      <h1 class="mt-4 font-black leading-[0.92] text-[13vw] text-center text-ink sm:text-7xl lg:text-[5.75rem]">
        Publish it.<br class="sm:hidden"> Send it. Own it.
      </h1>

      <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-3xl text-center text-xl sm:text-2xl deck">
        Your publication, your newsletter and your paying subscribers, on software you run — with nobody standing between you and the people who read you.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-6 rule-thin"></div>
      <p class="py-2 text-center byline">By the staff &middot; Filed from your own machine &middot; MIT licensed</p>
      <div class="rule-thick"></div>
    </section>

    <!-- The lede and the boxed insert, set the way a column and a well are -->
    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,7fr)_minmax(0,5fr)] pb-14 pt-8">
      <div class="copy">
        <div class="leading-relaxed text-body columns-print">
          <p class="m-0 dropcap">Every publishing platform you can sign up for makes the same trade: it hosts your words, and in return it holds your readers. The list is theirs, the payment relationship is theirs, and the terms are whatever they happen to be this quarter.</p>
          <p class="m-0 mt-4">The Open Times is the other arrangement. It is one program, on one machine you control, that renders the page, sends the email, takes the payment and files the announcement to every network you post to. One action does all four.</p>
          <p class="m-0 mt-4">There is no platform fee, because there is no platform — only your database, your mail provider, your Stripe account and your domain.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 items-center mt-8">
          <a class="inline-flex items-center px-6 h-12 text-sm ink-button" href="/login" data-stx-link>Start your paper</a>
          <a class="inline-flex gap-2 items-center px-6 h-12 text-sm ink-button ink-button--ghost" href="https://github.com/stacksjs/opentimes">
            <span class="h-4 w-4 i-simple-icons-github" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            Read the source
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!--
        The insert. A single published story carrying the whole product: the
        page it made, the mail it sent, and the wires it went out on. Boxed and
        captioned, because that is what a newspaper does with a picture.
      -->
      <figure class="m-0 self-start">
        <div class="bg-panel border-2 border-ink" role="img" aria-label="A story published to a custom domain, mailed to 4,182 subscribers and wired to six networks">
          <div class="flex gap-3 items-baseline justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-ink">
            <span class="text-on-accent folio">The Weekly Build</span>
            <span class="text-on-accent folio">theweeklybuild.dev</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5">
            <p class="m-0 font-bold leading-tight text-2xl text-ink">What shipping every Friday for a year actually cost me</p>
            <p class="m-0 mt-2.5 leading-relaxed text-body text-sm">Fifty-one issues, two rewrites, and one week I nearly stopped. The honest version of the ledger.</p>

            <div class="grid gap-2.5 mt-5 pt-4 rule-thin">
              <div class="flex gap-3 items-center">
                <span class="shrink-0 h-4 w-4 text-accent i-hugeicons-mail-01" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="text-body text-sm">Mailed to 4,182 subscribers</span>
              </div>
              <div class="flex gap-3 items-center">
                <span class="shrink-0 h-4 w-4 text-accent i-hugeicons-share-08" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 items-center text-body text-sm">
                  On the wire to
                  <span class="inline-flex gap-1.5 items-center text-ink">
                    <span class="h-4 w-4 i-simple-icons-bluesky" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="h-4 w-4 i-simple-icons-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="h-4 w-4 i-simple-icons-linkedin" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="h-4 w-4 i-simple-icons-instagram" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="h-4 w-4 i-simple-icons-threads" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="h-4 w-4 i-simple-icons-mastodon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  </span>
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mt-2 byline">One publish &mdash; the page, the send and six announcements.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
  </article>

  <!-- The wire: the networks a story goes out on -->
  <section class="bg-panel-2 border-ink border-y-2" aria-label="Supported networks">
    <ul class="sr-only">
      <li>Bluesky</li><li>X</li><li>LinkedIn</li><li>Instagram</li><li>Threads</li><li>Mastodon</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="mx-auto px-6 max-w-[1400px]">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:gap-10 sm:items-center py-5">
        <p class="m-0 shrink-0 kicker">On the wire</p>
        <div class="overflow-hidden relative grow [mask-image:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent,#000_7%,#000_93%,transparent)]">
          <ul class="flex gap-12 items-center w-max marquee-track" aria-hidden="true">
            <ProviderChip icon="bluesky" name="Bluesky" />
            <ProviderChip icon="x" name="X" />
            <ProviderChip icon="linkedin" name="LinkedIn" />
            <ProviderChip icon="instagram" name="Instagram" />
            <ProviderChip icon="threads" name="Threads" />
            <ProviderChip icon="mastodon" name="Mastodon" />
            <ProviderChip icon="bluesky" name="Bluesky" />
            <ProviderChip icon="x" name="X" />
            <ProviderChip icon="linkedin" name="LinkedIn" />
            <ProviderChip icon="instagram" name="Instagram" />
            <ProviderChip icon="threads" name="Threads" />
            <ProviderChip icon="mastodon" name="Mastodon" />
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Story 02 · The publication -->
  <section id="publish" class="mx-auto px-6 py-16 sm:py-20 max-w-[1400px]">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,5fr)_minmax(0,7fr)]">
      <div class="max-w-md reveal">
        <SectionLabel index="02" label="The publication" />
        <h2 class="mt-3 leading-[1.02] text-4xl text-ink sm:text-5xl">A paper you are<br>not renting.</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 rule-thin"></div>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-body copy">Long-form stories render at your own domain, on templates that are files in your project. The archive is a table you can query, back up and move.</p>
        <a class="inline-flex gap-2 items-center mt-6 font-semibold text-accent text-sm group" href="/features/publications" data-stx-link>
          How publications work
          <span class="h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5 i-hugeicons-arrow-right-01" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Three steps as a numbered ledger. Deliberately not cards: this is a
          sequence, and cards would flatten it into three equal things. -->
      <ol class="grid gap-0 m-0 p-0 list-none border-line border-t divide-line divide-y reveal">
        <li class="grid gap-2 sm:gap-6 sm:grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] py-6">
          <span class="font-mono text-muted text-sm">01</span>
          <div class="max-w-[54ch]">
            <h3 class="m-0 text-ink text-xl">Write the piece</h3>
            <p class="m-0 mt-2 leading-relaxed text-body">The same composer handles a two-line note and a three-thousand-word essay. Long-form gets a title, a slug and an archive entry.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid gap-2 sm:gap-6 sm:grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] py-6">
          <span class="font-mono text-muted text-sm">02</span>
          <div class="max-w-[54ch]">
            <h3 class="m-0 text-ink text-xl">Decide who reads it</h3>
            <p class="m-0 mt-2 leading-relaxed text-body">Free for everyone, subscribers only, or paying subscribers only. A choice per story rather than a plan you commit to.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid gap-2 sm:gap-6 sm:grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] py-6">
          <span class="font-mono text-muted text-sm">03</span>
          <div class="max-w-[54ch]">
            <h3 class="m-0 text-ink text-xl">Put it to bed</h3>
            <p class="m-0 mt-2 leading-relaxed text-body">The page goes live, the email goes out, and the announcement goes to every network you post to. One action covers all three.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Story 03 · The mail and the money, as two facing panels of unequal weight -->
  <section class="mx-auto pb-16 px-6 sm:pb-20 max-w-[1400px]">
    <div class="grid gap-px lg:grid-cols-2 bg-ink border-2 border-ink reveal">
      <div class="grid content-between gap-8 p-7 sm:p-9 bg-bg">
        <div class="max-w-[44ch]">
          <p class="m-0 kicker">The mail</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 leading-tight text-3xl text-ink">Publishing a story is sending it.</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-body copy">Mail goes out through your own provider, so deliverability, reputation and cost per email all stay yours. Export the list whenever you want — it was never held anywhere else.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="inline-flex gap-2 items-center font-semibold text-accent text-sm group" href="/features/newsletter" data-stx-link>
          How sending works
          <span class="h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5 i-hugeicons-arrow-right-01" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="grid content-between gap-8 p-7 sm:p-9 text-on-accent bg-ink">
        <div class="max-w-[44ch]">
          <p class="m-0 text-on-accent/70 kicker">The money</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 leading-tight text-3xl text-on-accent">Charge for it. Keep all of it.</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-on-accent/70">Readers pay into your Stripe account. The only fee is the one Stripe charges you directly, because there is nobody else in the transaction.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="inline-flex gap-2 items-center font-semibold text-on-accent text-sm group" href="/features/paid-subscriptions" data-stx-link>
          How payments work
          <span class="h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5 i-hugeicons-arrow-right-01" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Story 04 · Discover, set as a classified index -->
  <section id="discover" class="bg-panel-2 border-line border-y">
    <div class="mx-auto px-6 py-16 sm:py-20 max-w-[1400px]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center reveal">
        <SectionLabel index="03" label="The exchange" />
        <h2 class="mt-3 leading-[1.02] text-4xl text-ink sm:text-5xl">Found by people who already read.</h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl leading-relaxed text-body copy">Papers recommend each other. A reader who trusts one writer sees the handful that writer vouches for — ranked by subscriptions rather than by spend.</p>
      </div>

      <ul class="grid gap-0 m-0 mt-10 mx-auto p-0 max-w-3xl list-none border-ink border-t-2 divide-line divide-y reveal">
        <li class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-1 items-baseline justify-between py-4">
          <span class="grid gap-0.5">
